# Power-release #3 — make AHA#2.1 landable.
# Apply on Delta (sigil builds there): `git apply docs/patches/iter3-toobig-no-bench.patch`
# then: `fluxc test --package sigil-top` (NEVER raw cargo; NEVER build on Epsilon/Beta).
#
# Goal: a too-big (over-cap) chunk must SHRINK the request window and retry the same
# peer — never be counted as got=0 and bench an innocent peer (the v0.39 12-MiB stall).
# Surgical: distinguish TooBig from Bad/garbage at the decode + ingest boundary, and
# expose it so the frontier scheduler can branch. Probe paths (max_header_height /
# header_height_range) keep Option semantics — a probe miss never benches/stalls.
--- a/crates/sigil-top/src/block_sync.rs
